---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Disclaimer"
	description="Non-commercial use statement and disclosures for APIs and data sources used on this site."
>
	<header class="section-head">
		<h1>Disclaimer</h1>
		<p>Non-commercial use and third-party data disclosures.</p>
	</header>

	<article class="about-prose disclaimer-prose">
		<section>
			<h2>Non-commercial use</h2>
			<p>
				This website is a personal project. I make absolutely no commercial use of any kind of this
				website. It is not operated as a business, does not sell products or services, does not
				carry paid advertising, and is not used to generate revenue.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Personal opinions</h2>
			<p>
				Recommendations, ratings, notes, and travel write-ups reflect my personal opinions and
				experiences only. They are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any film studio,
				publisher, award body, platform, or brand mentioned here.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>APIs and data sources</h2>
			<p>
				Some metadata, images, and maps on this site are loaded from third-party services. Those
				providers retain their rights in their data and branding. This site is not endorsed or
				certified by any of them. Where a provider asks for attribution or a required notice, it
				appears on relevant pages and is summarized below.
			</p>

			<h3>TMDB (The Movie Database)</h3>
			<p>
				Movie metadata and posters may come from
				<a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>TMDB<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB. Use of TMDB
				materials is subject to TMDB’s terms and attribution requirements.
			</p>

			<h3>Open Library</h3>
			<p>
				Book metadata and covers may come from
				<a href="https://openlibrary.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Open Library<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Open Library is a project of the Internet Archive.
			</p>

			<h3>Wikidata</h3>
			<p>
				Film and book award / accolade data and some Wikipedia link resolution may use
				<a href="https://www.wikidata.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Wikidata<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Structured data from Wikidata is available under
				<a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>CC0<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Credit is appreciated and shown where award data appears.
			</p>

			<h3>Wikipedia</h3>
			<p>
				“More info” / Wikipedia links point to articles on
				<a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Wikipedia<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Wikipedia text is typically available under Creative Commons licenses; this site links to
				Wikipedia pages rather than reproducing article text. Wikipedia® is a registered trademark of
				the Wikimedia Foundation.
			</p>

			<h3>Unsplash</h3>
			<p>
				Some trip cover photos may come from
				<a href="https://unsplash.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Unsplash<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>, subject to the Unsplash License and API guidelines.
			</p>

			<h3>OpenStreetMap &amp; Leaflet</h3>
			<p>
				Maps may use
				<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>OpenStreetMap<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>
				data (© OpenStreetMap contributors) and the
				<a href="https://leafletjs.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Leaflet<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>
				library. Place search in admin uses
				<a href="https://nominatim.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Nominatim<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Map tiles, geodata, and geocoding remain subject to their respective licenses and terms.
			</p>

			<h3>IMDb, Goodreads &amp; marketplace ratings</h3>
			<p>
				Links to IMDb or Goodreads (when present) are outbound references only. Community scores shown
				next to my personal rating may come from TMDB, IMDb (via OMDb when configured), Open Library,
				and/or Google Books. Those scores belong to their respective platforms; this site does not
				scrape prohibited sources for content and is not affiliated with them. My star rating is always
				my own opinion.
			</p>

			<h3>Google Books</h3>
			<p>
				Some book community ratings may come from the
				<a href="https://developers.google.com/books" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Google Books API<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. Google and Google Books are trademarks of Google LLC.
			</p>

			<h3>OMDb (optional)</h3>
			<p>
				When an OMDb API key is configured, film community ratings from IMDb may be fetched via
				<a href="https://www.omdbapi.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>OMDb<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
				>. OMDb is not affiliated with IMDb.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Trademarks</h2>
			<p>
				Names such as Oscar® / Academy Awards®, Golden Globe®, BAFTA, Pulitzer®, Booker Prize, and
				other award titles are trademarks of their respective owners. Mentions and simple visual
				markers on this site are for identification of publicly reported awards only and do not imply
				endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Accuracy</h2>
			<p>
				Third-party data can be incomplete or outdated. I do not guarantee that titles, dates,
				covers, awards, map locations, or linked pages are always correct. If something looks wrong,
				feel free to
				<a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about this disclaimer or the site:
				<a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
